     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many references. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPlease check what was intended. A few possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum, and it may be what was meant.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **500 mg three times daily.** This is 1,500 mg/day, a more conservative option.\n- **1,700 mg total daily.** This could be split into divided doses, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note that the dose exceeds the usual maximum."
      }
     ],
